  "notes": "Difficult verse. tryudāyam (tri-udāyam) is unclear; rendered literally as 'with threefold offering'. yathā vaḥ stomaḥ is read 'as it is yours (the praise)'; the exact construction is uncertain. uparāsu 'later/upper' of vikṣu and bṛhaddiveṣu (a group name, 'those of lofty heaven') are uncertain. yuṣme sacā: yuṣme is a locative-type form with sacā 'together with you'; the form is uncertain.",
